      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{64873f159cf028090ce2c2e2|full_name}: It's happening to me with the Vive Wireless adapter, so it may be that specifically and yes it happens every time.  All you need to do when using a Vive headset with the wireless adapter is pull the battery, plug it back in, and when your Vive headset powers back up and reconnects the audio input options will be cleared in the audio settings. \n\nI suspect what may be happening is (I assume) VRChat may be polling for audio devices when the headset turns on, but it's getting nothing back because it detects the headset, but the headset hasn't powered up enough/completely to tell it what the available audio inputs and outputs are, so the VRChat client just shrugs and loads nothing.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
